# Header rules for ck-cdn. Natively supported by Workers static assets.
#
# This host serves bytes and nothing else. It knows nothing about who is
# asking — no auth, no tenancy, no tier. Keep it that way: the moment a
# rule here depends on the caller, the CDN has become an application.

# ── Fonts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The widget is injected into other people's sites, so every asset it
# pulls is a cross-origin request. Fonts in particular are fetched in
# CORS mode by the browser regardless of crossorigin= on the tag, and a
# response without Access-Control-Allow-Origin is discarded silently —
# the widget would just render in the fallback face on every customer
# site while looking fine on ours.
#
# A placeholder rather than a literal /v1/, so the next major inherits
# this the day it is created. Forgetting to add a rule for /v2/fonts/
# would be that same silent failure, on a path nobody thinks to check.
/:major/fonts/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Widget ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One path. The major is in the URL because this string gets pasted into
# other people's HTML and can never be changed afterwards — a breaking
# change bumps WIDGET_MAJOR in config/origins.js and /v1/ keeps serving
# the old build for everyone who already installed it.
#
# Ten minutes is short enough that a fix reaches every tenant the same
# day, and long enough that a busy site is not revalidating on every
# page view.
/v1/widget.js
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, must-revalidate

# ── Brand ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Favicons, logos and the OG image. Referenced by absolute URL from
# other people's link previews, so CORS-open and cached for a week —
# these are not content-hashed, so a year would be too long to correct
# a bad OG image.
/brand/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
